      "message": "fix(motion): a deburr leaves each edge run straight up before travelling\n\nEach run opened with a rapid from the previous run's end - cone still in\nthe break it cut - diagonally to the next start at the clearance plane,\nthrough the part (#304). The path now retracts vertically first, the\nsame move it already made after the last run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
